  "preamble": "Denasalization of the open-mid nasal vowel [ɛ̃] to oral [ɛ]. Proto-Slavic *ę, reconstructed as [ɛ̃ː], lost its nasality in Bulgarian and Macedonian, giving [ɛ] (*pętь > пет 'five', *męso > месо 'meat'). In modern Polish, nasal ę /ɛ̃/ is pronounced as oral [ɛ] word-finally (będę, idę) and before /l/ and /w/ (wzięli, zaczęli).",
  "phoneticEffects": "Denasalization",
  "languageExamples": [
    {
      "language": "Polish",
      "languageFamily": "West Slavic",
      "isAllophone": true,
      "context": "Word-final ę, and ę before /l/ and /w/",
      "examples": [
        {
          "from": "będę 'I will be' with final ę",
          "to": "[ˈbɛndɛ]",
          "note": "Word-final ę is pronounced as oral [ɛ]; the careful pronunciation /ˈbɛn.dɛw̃/ keeps a nasal glide."
        },
        {
          "from": "idę 'I go' with final ę",
          "to": "/ˈi.dɛ/"
        },
        {
          "from": "wzięli 'they took (masc. pers.)', with ę before /l/",
          "to": "/ˈvʑɛ.li/",
          "note": "Before /l/ and /w/ ę loses its nasality altogether."
        },
        {
          "from": "zaczęli 'they began (masc. pers.)', with ę before /l/",
          "to": "/zaˈt͡ʂɛ.li/"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "Bulgarian",
      "languageFamily": "South Slavic",
      "examples": [
        {
          "from": "Proto-Slavic *pętь, Old Church Slavonic пѧть 'five'",
          "to": "пет [pɛt]",
          "note": "The front nasal vowel *ę denasalized to [ɛ]; dialectal пен preserves a trace of the nasal."
        },
        {
          "from": "Proto-Slavic *męso, Old Church Slavonic мѧсо 'meat'",
          "to": "месо [mɛˈsɔ]"
        }
      ]
    },
